From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tamnd <tamnd@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 22:55:25 +0800
Subject: build: give the allocator selects a windows arm

`//bazel/internal:tcmalloc_numa_aware` and `:tcmalloc_want_numa_aware` are
`select()`s over Linux and macOS with no other arms, and AsyncRT depends on both
unconditionally, so they are two of the first analysis failures on the way to any
Windows target.

Neither allocator is portable here. tcmalloc as patched in this tree wants glibc
restartable sequences and reads NUMA topology out of sysfs, both from patches
carried in `bazel/public-patches`, and there is no upstream Windows port to fall
back to. gperftools, which is what the macOS arm uses, has no Windows build in
the prebuilt archive this tree fetches either.

So point both arms at `:empty_lib` and let the platform allocator do the work.
That is a real performance loss and not a papering over, so the comment says
which two Linux specific things stand in the way rather than just noting that it
is unsupported. The macOS arm of `tcmalloc_want_numa_aware` already resolves to
`:empty_lib` for the same shape of reason, so this follows a pattern that is
already here.

Signed-off-by: tamnd <1218621+tamnd@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 bazel/internal/BUILD.bazel | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/bazel/internal/BUILD.bazel b/bazel/internal/BUILD.bazel
index dc4d8098c3..55711faf6e 100644
--- a/bazel/internal/BUILD.bazel
+++ b/bazel/internal/BUILD.bazel
@@ -232,6 +232,11 @@ alias(
         "@platforms//os:macos": "@gperftools-macos//:tcmalloc",
         # NOTE: This library doesn't override new/free globally, which the default library does
         "@platforms//os:linux": "@tcmalloc//tcmalloc:tcmalloc_internal_methods_only_numa_aware",
+        # Neither allocator builds here. tcmalloc as patched in this tree needs glibc
+        # restartable sequences and reads NUMA topology out of sysfs, and gperftools
+        # has no Windows build either. Fall back to the system allocator, which is
+        # correct but slower, until a replacement lands.
+        "@platforms//os:windows": ":empty_lib",
     }),
 )
 
@@ -243,6 +248,8 @@ alias(
     actual = select({
         "@platforms//os:macos": ":empty_lib",
         "@platforms//os:linux": "@tcmalloc//tcmalloc:want_numa_aware",
+        # Nothing to turn on when there is no tcmalloc to turn it on in.
+        "@platforms//os:windows": ":empty_lib",
     }),
 )
 
